From 596259edaf613321ee18332ae59b6a21243e0323 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:24:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AmgX: aggregation multigrid in the default configurations

The option Multigrid of the AmgX preconditioner and of AmgXPCG selects
the algebraic multigrid of their default configurations: Classical (the
current one, by default) or Aggregation, the multigrid of the
configuration PCG_AGGREGATION_JACOBI of AmgX (aggregates of size two,
three sweeps of a damped block Jacobi smoother), without writing a
configuration of AmgX. Like the verbosity level and the parameters of
AmgX, it is refused with a configuration given. AmgXSolverTest solves with
AmgXPCG and with the conjugate gradient of MFEM preconditioned by AmgX
with the aggregation multigrid, and checks the refusals.
---
 docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst | 11 ++-
 docs/source/user_guide/linear_solvers.rst     |  6 +-
 src/AmgXSolvers.cxx                           | 87 +++++++++++++++----
 tests/AmgXSolverTest.cxx                      | 33 +++++++
 4 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

